      "side": 1,
      "message": "Assumption 1): yes. If someone does manage to make a custom SkCodec object (I\u0027ve never seen it done), then we\u0027ll break them and that\u0027s ok. All our major clients will use one of the two \"pre-baked\" options.\n\nAssumption 2): Yes, that might happen. Your suggestion sounds somewhat nice, but I\u0027d really rather not flood the `SkPngEncoder` namespace with helpers beyond what we have. We already have one there that has the option for different compressions, and more seems... superfluous.",
      "parentUuid": "a55b345a_7b943995",
      "revId": "9529ec2c0dd174527fa9ded88f4ca6bde0219e87",
